---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title={`About — ${SITE_NAME}`} description={`What ${SITE_NAME} is, how the reviews are made and what the ratings mean.`}>
  <div class="about">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <p class="page-lead">
      I write notes in Notion when I finish a book. The site collects them
      automatically every day, so what you read here is what I actually thought
      about the book.
    </p>

    <h2 class="about-heading">The ratings</h2>
    <dl class="scale">
      <div><dt>10</dt><dd>One of the best I’ve read. Read it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>8–9</dt><dd>Very good. Recommended.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>6–7</dt><dd>Good, but with weaknesses.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>4–5</dt><dd>Some good ideas, but a lot to get through to find them.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>1–3</dt><dd>Skip it.</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="about-note">
      Most of the earliest reviews are in Norwegian, and some are partly summarized by AI.
      New reviews are in English, and I write them myself.
      To hear about new books, you can follow along via <a href={`${base}rss.xml`}>RSS</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
